            ("bio_microscopy", "Light microscopes magnify up to about fifteen hundred times with a resolution of around two hundred nanometres, while electron microscopes resolve down to roughly 0.1 nanometres. Magnification is calculated as image size divided by actual size.", "What is the formula for magnification?"),
            ("bio_organelles", "Ribosomes synthesise proteins. The rough endoplasmic reticulum carries ribosomes and folds new proteins. The Golgi apparatus modifies, sorts and packages proteins into vesicles for secretion, and lysosomes contain digestive enzymes that break down waste material.", "What does the Golgi apparatus do?"),
