            ("gen_mutation", "Mutations are changes in the DNA base sequence. Point mutations include substitutions, insertions and deletions, and insertions or deletions cause frameshifts. Sickle cell anaemia is caused by a single base substitution in the gene for the beta chain of haemoglobin.", "What causes sickle cell anaemia?"),
            ("gen_mendel", "Gregor Mendel studied inheritance in pea plants. A monohybrid cross between two heterozygous parents gives a phenotype ratio of three dominant to one recessive. Alleles are different versions of a gene, and an organism with two identical alleles is homozygous.", "What ratio does a monohybrid cross give?"),
